    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d742">

                <pb facs="0643" n="631" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg631"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890D.00/910: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-09-04T17:00:00+01:00">September 4,
                            1942—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4944. In talking with Mr. Eden this morning he told me that he hoped our
                    representative at Beirut in talking with General de Gaulle would discourage him
                    in an anti-British policy in Syria and the Lebanon.</p>
                <p>Mr. Eden also said that he understood Wadsworth<anchor n="66" xml:id="d742-f1"/>
                    is being sent to Beirut which he very much approved and asked me if I would
                    inquire how soon Wadsworth would reach his destination.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d742-f1" n="66" xml:id="d742-f1-content">
                <p>George Wadsworth, appointed American Diplomatic Agent and Consul General in Syria
                    and in Lebanon; for correspondence on this subject, see <ref target="#pg641">pp.
                        641</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
